1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,866
This video shows you how to work with the items of an array: keep some,

2
00:00:06,866 --> 00:00:09,270
change them, and add them up.

3
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:12,480
This pipeline reads AWS CloudTrail.

4
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:16,150
Its Parser step reads each record.

5
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:21,310
One record holds an array of API calls, in Records.

6
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:22,621
Add a Code step.

7
00:00:22,621 --> 00:00:26,372
Records is a variant, so give it a type.

8
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:29,064
It's an array of objects.

9
00:00:29,064 --> 00:00:34,430
Name the fields you use: eventName and errorCode are strings.

10
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:39,481
filter keeps the items for which your function is true.

11
00:00:39,481 --> 00:00:43,391
In r => r.errorCode != null, r is one call.

12
00:00:43,391 --> 00:00:48,310
Keep the calls that failed: those with an errorCode.

13
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:52,190
This record has six calls, and one failed.

14
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:55,936
map replaces each item with your function's value.

15
00:00:55,936 --> 00:00:59,190
Keep only the name of each failed call.

16
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:01,857
Now failed is an array of names.

17
00:01:01,857 --> 00:01:06,390
Records is unchanged: filter and map give new arrays.

18
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:10,420
For a total, visit each call with for...of.

19
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:13,334
Add up the bytes S3 sent.

20
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:20,583
Name the byte count in the type too.

21
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:26,458
Only calls to S3 have a byte count.

22
00:01:26,458 --> 00:01:29,950
For the others, two question marks give zero.

23
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,310
bytes_out is the total for each record.

24
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:35,112
Save.

25
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:40,121
Check on learning.

26
00:01:40,321 --> 00:01:42,989
What does filter give?

27
00:01:47,389 --> 00:01:51,465
A new array of the items for which its expression is true.

28
00:01:51,465 --> 00:01:54,314
The original array is unchanged.

29
00:01:55,214 --> 00:01:57,390
No function adds up an array.

30
00:01:57,390 --> 00:02:00,992
How do you total a value over its items?

31
00:02:05,392 --> 00:02:10,389
Visit each item with for...of, and add its value to a total.

32
00:02:11,289 --> 00:02:15,207
Next, you turn array items into records.
